The query uses a sub‑query with UNION to capture both conditions without any EXISTS sub‑queries, allowing the planner to leverage indexes on :Person(name) and :Company(name). The final RETURN counts distinct companies that satisfy either condition.

Executed Cypher query:
// Ensure indexes exist for fast name look‑ups:
// CREATE INDEX ON :Person(name);
// CREATE INDEX ON :Company(name);

CALL {
    // Companies founded by Sergey Brin
    MATCH (c:Company)-[:foundedBy]->(p:Person {name: 'Sergey Brin'})
    RETURN c
    UNION
    // Companies that are the parent of Jambool (i.e., Jambool is a subsidiary)
    MATCH (j:Company {name: 'Jambool'})-[:subsidiaryOf]->(c:Company)
    RETURN c
}
RETURN count(DISTINCT c) AS companyCount;


